1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martha arrived to the US on October 15, 1923, via the Bergensfjord, at Ellis Island, NY with $25 in her pocket. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berjensfjord: Built by Cammell Laird & Company, Birkenhead, England, 1913. 11,013 gross tons; 530 (bp) feet long; 61 feet wide. Steam quadruple expansion engines, twin screw.  Service speed 15 knots.  1,200 passengers (100 first c
2 CONC lass, 250 second class, 850 third class).
2 CONT
2 CONT Built for Norwegian-America Line, Norwegian flag, in 1913 and named Bergensfjord. Oslo-New York service. Troopship 1940-46. Sold to Home Lines, Panamanian flag, in 1946 and renamed Aregentina. Mediterranean-South America and Medit
2 CONC erranean-New York service. Sold to Zim Line, Israeli flag, in 1953 and renamed Jerusalem. Mediterranean-New York service. Renamed Aliya in 1957. Laid up 1958-59. Scrapped in Italy in 1959.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Kilde:  Digitale kirkebøker – Østfold – Skjeberg i Skjeberg – Klokkebok nr. 12 (1901-1924) – Fødte og døpte, side 15.
